Setup
-----
R packages:      install.packages("remotes"); remotes::install_deps(dependencies = TRUE)
Python packages: pip install -r requirements.txt
USDA API key:    add `FDC_API_KEY=your_key` to ~/.Renviron (see config/usda_config.yml)
Data locations:  edit config/paths.yml (raw data dir, active dataset)

Layout
------
instruments/<name>/   instrument-specific (e.g. the FFQ form); changes or disappears with another input source
                      questionnaire.csv, frequency_factors.yml
datasets/<name>/      dataset-specific: data dictionaries, dataset.yml, var_map.csv (var -> q_id),
                      food_items.csv = USDA batch-search input (instrument + dictionary + hand-written search terms)
R/, python/, config/  generic, functional code (no process logic):
                      R/ helper functions; python/build_food_items.py, python/fndds_match.py
scripts/              process code: the analysis steps that call the functions above

food_items.csv is the interface: any input source that produces the same columns
(var, form_label, portion, search_terms, exclude, ...) can use the pipeline unchanged.
Rebuild it after changing the questionnaire or var_map (hand-edited columns are kept):
    python3 python/build_food_items.py datasets/perls9

FNDDS matching: layers
----------------------
client (per dataset)   datasets/<name>/: food_items.csv -> fndds_match/ (results, review sheet)
                       knows nothing about FNDDS files, indexes or models
server (one instance)  config/server.yml + server/ (not in git):
                         reference/fndds/<release>/ + registry.json   FNDDS releases, active release
                         indexes/<release>/<model>/                   offline FAISS index
                         models/registry.json                         embedding / reranker models
                         feedback/events.jsonl                        feedback from all datasets
                         runs/<run_id>/                               manifest + candidates of every request
interface              dietcali.server.MatchService (in-process now; maps to HTTP endpoints later)

Code: python/dietcali/{core, server, client}; command-line entry points in python/.
Tests: python -m pytest tests

Server jobs
  python python/server_update_fndds.py                  check for a new FNDDS release, download + register it
                                                        (first release is activated; later ones are not)
         ... --import-dir data_raw/fndds/<folder> --name 2024-10-31   use an existing download
         ... --status | --check | --activate <release>
  python python/server_build_index.py [--release R] [--model M]      build the FAISS index
  python python/server_evaluate.py --run <run_id>                    score a run against expert feedback
  python python/server_evaluate.py --dataset perls9 --release R [--model M] [--rerank]
                                                        score a new release / model before activating it

Client (per dataset)
  1. python python/fndds_match.py [--sources bm25 dense api] [--rerank]
     -> datasets/<name>/fndds_match/matches.csv (review sheet), runs/<run_id>/
  2. review matches.csv: review_status = accept | correct | none, manual_fdc_id for `correct`, review_note
  3. python python/record_feedback.py --reviewer <name>      (sends the decisions to the server)

Pipeline steps
--------------
1. read in data
2. ID correction
4. check var names and added var labels (pre=process)
5. derive nutrient density
6. convert to servings per day (FFQ config)
7. food group 
8. nutrient derivation for whole grain
9. servings per day to gram per day?
10. derived required nurtrients (need nutrient list)
11. merge FFQ and nutrients with new var added
12. to calculate different eating indexes: index specific algorithm